WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:06.370
Margot Robbie, Emma Mackey, Margot Mackey,
Emma Robbie: You wouldn't be the first person

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:11.559
to get these two actors mixed up — and even
Barbie had something to say about their resemblance…before

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:12.645
the line got cut.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:16.002
Some celebrities just really, really look
alike.

00:00:16.002 --> 00:00:19.140
"I'm seeing double, here — four Krustys!"

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:24.425
Isla Fisher once put Amy Adams' face on her
own Christmas cards to see if anybody would notice.

00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:29.340
Bryce Dallas Howard and Jessica Chastain apparently
spend inordinate amounts of time insisting

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.937
that they're not the same person.

00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:35.640
And if you've ever watched Netflix's original
series Sex Education, you'll know that star

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:40.260
Emma Mackey, who plays Maeve, bears a striking
resemblance to Barbie star and Academy Award

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:41.838
nominee Margot Robbie.

00:00:41.838 --> 00:00:45.829
In fact, it was their resemblance that led
to Mackey appearing in the Barbie movie, and

00:00:45.829 --> 00:00:49.509
an early version of the film even acknowledged
their similar looks.

00:00:49.509 --> 00:00:52.939
According to Robbie, this moment had to be
cut from the final product.

00:00:52.939 --> 00:00:56.930
Speaking to Buzzfeed during one of their patented
"puppy interviews," Robbie said:

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.710
"She plays one of the Barbies in the movie,
pretty much because Greta [Gerwig] and I thought

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:01.820
it would be funny."

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:05.440
Gerwig and Robbie actually came up with a
joke about the pair's similar appearances,

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.335
but when all was said and done, it didn't
land the way they thought it would.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:12.800
"We were going to do this whole joke about
us looking similar [...] and once we got all

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:16.996
dressed up as our Barbies, we were kind of
like, 'We don't actually look that similar.'"

00:01:16.996 --> 00:01:21.119
As it turned out, the two actors don't look
all that similar when one is rocking blonde

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:22.843
hair and the other's a brunette.

00:01:22.843 --> 00:01:24.793
"So we didn't put that joke in the movie.

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:29.314
But when people come up to me and say, 'I
loved you in Sex Education,' I just say thank you."

00:01:29.314 --> 00:01:33.920
Maeve Wiley, Mackey's character on Sex Education,
changes up her hair color a lot throughout

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.439
the show, and it's worth acknowledging that,
as a blonde, she definitely resembles Robbie.

00:01:38.439 --> 00:01:42.700
The joke clearly didn't land on the Barbie
set due to Mackey's natural hue, so it's probably

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:44.953
for the best that they didn't bother forcing
it.

00:01:44.953 --> 00:01:49.369
Nevertheless, Mackey is a key part of the
final product as Physicist Barbie, one of

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:53.560
the residents of Barbieland with whom Robbie's
Stereotypical Barbie spends time throughout

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:54.255
the film.

00:01:54.255 --> 00:01:59.159
In fact, Margot Robbie first met Emma Mackey
around the time they were both cast in Barbie.

00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:03.220
So maybe it's not surprising that only after
the fact did they decide they didn't resemble

00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:05.135
one another enough to joke about it.

00:02:05.135 --> 00:02:09.270
Robbie briefly detailed what it was like working
with Mackey during a filmed interview for

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:11.266
SiriusXM's The Jess Cagle Show.

00:02:11.266 --> 00:02:15.530
While discussing a prank of sorts Ryan Gosling
played on the rest of the cast during filming

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.440
of the movie's girl's night scene, Robbie
recounted feeling nostalgic about childhood

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:23.773
sleepovers while brushing her teeth in a mirror
alongside Mackey's Physicist Barbie.

00:02:23.773 --> 00:02:28.617
"Then we shared a bed, and I was like, 'we
only met like two weeks ago.

00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:31.974
We bonded so quickly, and I think the sleepover
had a little to do with it."

00:02:31.974 --> 00:02:36.530
According to Robbie's Buzzfeed interview,
she and Greta Gerwig offered Mackey a part

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.637
in Barbie at least in part based on her famous
resemblance to Robbie.

00:02:39.637 --> 00:02:43.670
Even though that didn't end up informing their
characters' relationship in the film, it seems

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:48.970
the two got along well on set all the same,
allowing Mackey to remain a part of its ensemble cast.

